Thanks @thePanz for your patience since April. I finished the PR along the lines of that comment, keeping your authorship; the two methods became one:

```php
[$min, $max] = $factory->createBoundaries($time);
```

Beyond taste, the pair shape fixes a latent bug in the two-method version: `createWithRandomMin()` and `createWithRandomMax()` each called `create()`, so calling them back to back without an explicit time could land on two different milliseconds and produce a range that silently excludes ULIDs. Both bounds now derive from a single created ULID, and a test pins that they share the timestamp even without an explicit time.

The second half of my own suggestion, a new interface implemented by both the Ulid and Uuid factories, I am dropping as speculative: `UuidFactory::create()` returns whatever version is configured, and boundaries only mean something for the time-based ones, so the interface would need conditional semantics nobody has asked for. The Uuid side can come with a concrete use case.

Also added the missing tests and the CHANGELOG entry. Uid is green at 215 tests, and restoring the previous factory fails the 2 new ones.

